  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feed the Child and Starve the Cancer</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To provide nutritional assistance to children with Cancer who are from poor to extremely poor families. Most of these families cannot afford a protein-rich diet for their children. Fresh and dry fruits along with nuts in the diet of a child fighting cancer can make a huge difference.  (16% between the first and the last visit of the child to the hospital). While in the city for treatment an earning member of the family becomes a full-time attendee for the patient. We provide meals for them too.</narrative>
  </description>
